course: dictionary
lesson: 14091
title: Words that change over time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mellowed is a word about change over time. When something mellows, it becomes softer, calmer, or less harsh. «Grandad has mellowed since he retired.» Grandad used to get cross quickly, but now he is gentler. Mellowed means became calmer and kinder.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The old brick walls had mellowed in the sun for a hundred years.» Years of sunshine have made the walls softer and warmer, not rough and bright. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Softer and warmer fits. Sharp and new does not.
explain: The same word works for light, sounds, and food. «The mellowed light of the autumn evening.» «The cheese had mellowed into a smooth, sweet taste.» Each one describes the same kind of change: from harsh to soft, or from sharp to rich and smooth.
fact: Mellowed is the past form of the verb mellow: mellow, mellows, mellowing, mellowed.
fact: «Mellowed» can mean became softer, calmer, and kinder with age or time.
fact: «Mellowed» can describe colours, sounds, or light that have become soft, warm, and rich, not harsh.
fact: «Mellowed» can describe fruit, wine, or cheese that has become ripe, sweet, and smooth.
fact: Mellowed can also be an adjective, as in «mellowed walls».
exercise: «Grandad has mellowed since he retired.» What does mellowed mean here? | Fell asleep | Got lost on the way home | *Became calmer and kinder | Became louder and angrier
exercise: «The old stone walls had mellowed in the sunshine.» Which word is closest in meaning to mellowed? | *softened | shouted | cracked | painted
exercise: «The cheese had mellowed into a sweet, smooth taste.» What kind of change does this describe? | It was frozen solid | It was thrown away | It turned hard and sour | *It became ripe and smooth
test: «The mellowed light of the autumn evening made the leaves glow.» What does mellowed describe? | Light that has gone out | A loud noise | Light that is bright and harsh | *Light that is soft and warm, not harsh
test: Mia says, «My big sister has mellowed since she went to college.» What does Mia mean? | Her sister has become ill | Her sister has left home for good | Her sister has lost her voice | *Her sister has become calmer and kinder
exam: Which word best fits? «The pears had ___ in the sun, and now they tasted sweet.» | Shouted | Cracked | *Mellowed | Frozen
